# satpulsewb with an explicit -L bind and no -T: -L takes the runner's allocated
# HTTP port and disables the access token (the ssh-tunnel workflow). The API is
# then open, but the CSRF content-type gate still guards state-changing POSTs.
# -d auto-connects over the FIFO the runner allocated.
-L
127.0.0.1:${SATPULSE_TEST_HTTP_PORT}
--no-open
-d
${SATPULSE_TEST_SERIAL}
